#: ../../../source/api/expression_tree/tree_util.rst:2
msgid "Tree utilities"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/api/expression_tree/tree_util.rst:4
msgid ""
"Tree rewriting accepts a single ``pybamm.Symbol`` root. To rewrite several "
"expressions with the same mapping, iterate explicitly and share a cache::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/api/expression_tree/tree_util.rst:7
msgid ""
"cache = {}\n"
"equations = {\n"
"    variable: pybamm.replace(equation, mapping, cache=cache)\n"
"    for variable, equation in model.rhs.items()\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/api/expression_tree/tree_util.rst:13
msgid ""
"The cache belongs to this mapping; use a fresh cache for a different "
"mapping. Model parameter processing remains available through "
"``parameter_values.process_model(model)``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/expression_tree/tree_util.py:docstring
#: of pybamm.expression_tree.tree_util.TreeDef:1
msgid ""
"The static structure of a symbol: everything needed to rebuild it from its "
"leaves. Returned by :func:`tree_flatten` and consumed by :func:"
"`tree_unflatten`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/api/expression_tree/tree_util.rst:0
msgid "Parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/expression_tree/tree_util.py:docstring
#: of pybamm.expression_tree.tree_util.TreeDef:4
msgid "The symbol class."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/expression_tree/tree_util.py:docstring
#: of pybamm.expression_tree.tree_util.TreeDef:6
msgid "How many leading leaves are the node's children."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/expression_tree/tree_util.py:docstring
#: of pybamm.expression_tree.tree_util.TreeDef:8
msgid "``list`` or ``tuple``, whichever the node stores its children in."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/expression_tree/tree_util.py:docstring
#: of pybamm.expression_tree.tree_util.TreeDef:10
msgid "``(field, kind, count, container)`` per extra leaf field, in order."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/expression_tree/tree_util.py:docstring
#: of pybamm.expression_tree.tree_util.TreeDef:12
msgid "The node's remaining (non-leaf, non-derived) state."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/expression_tree/tree_util.py:docstring
#: of pybamm.expression_tree.tree_util.tree_flatten:1
msgid ""
"Split a symbol into its leaves (children and the other symbols it depends "
"on) and a :class:`TreeDef` describing how to put it back together."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/expression_tree/tree_util.py:docstring
#: of pybamm.expression_tree.tree_util.tree_unflatten:1
msgid ""
"Rebuild a symbol from a :class:`TreeDef` and its leaves, without "
"simplification or validation. The result has no id yet."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/expression_tree/tree_util.py:docstring
#: of pybamm.expression_tree.tree_util.rebuild:1
msgid "Return ``node`` with its leaves swapped for ``new_leaves``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/expression_tree/tree_util.py:docstring
#: of pybamm.expression_tree.tree_util.rebuild:3
msgid ""
"``node`` itself is returned when no leaf changed, so untouched subtrees are "
"shared rather than copied. When only children changed the node's constructor "
"is used (so derived names, domains and, if ``simplify``, simplifications are "
"applied); otherwise the structure is rebuilt as-is with :func:"
"`tree_unflatten`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/expression_tree/tree_util.py:docstring
#: of pybamm.expression_tree.tree_util.tree_map:1
msgid "Rewrite an expression tree bottom-up, out of place."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/expression_tree/tree_util.py:docstring
#: of pybamm.expression_tree.tree_util.tree_map:3
msgid ""
"``fn(node, new_leaves)`` returns the node to use in place of ``node``, given "
"the already-rewritten leaves. Use :func:`rebuild` for the default \"same "
"node with new leaves\" behaviour."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/expression_tree/tree_util.py:docstring
#: of pybamm.expression_tree.tree_util.tree_map:7
msgid "The root of the expression tree to rewrite."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/expression_tree/tree_util.py:docstring
#: of pybamm.expression_tree.tree_util.tree_map:9
msgid ""
"Memo of ``{original node: rewritten node}``. Shared nodes are rewritten "
"once; pass the same dict across calls to share work between trees."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/expression_tree/tree_util.py:docstring
#: of pybamm.expression_tree.tree_util.tree_map:12
msgid ""
"``is_leaf(node)`` returning True stops the descent at ``node``: ``fn`` is "
"then called as ``fn(node, ())`` with nothing below it rewritten."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/api/expression_tree/tree_util.rst:0
msgid "Return type"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/expression_tree/tree_util.py:docstring
#: of pybamm.expression_tree.tree_util.tree_map:16
msgid "The rewritten symbol. ``tree`` is not modified."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/expression_tree/tree_util.py:docstring
#: of pybamm.expression_tree.tree_util.replace:1
msgid "Substitute symbols throughout an expression tree, out of place."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/expression_tree/tree_util.py:docstring
#: of pybamm.expression_tree.tree_util.replace:3
msgid ""
"Every node equal (by id) to a key of ``mapping`` is replaced by the "
"corresponding value, which is not itself traversed. All other nodes are "
"rebuilt with :func:`rebuild` only if something below them changed, so the "
"result shares every untouched subtree with ``tree``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/expression_tree/tree_util.py:docstring
#: of pybamm.expression_tree.tree_util.replace:8
msgid "The root of the expression tree to substitute into."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/expression_tree/tree_util.py:docstring
#: of pybamm.expression_tree.tree_util.replace:10
msgid "``{symbol: replacement}``; replacements may be numbers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/expression_tree/tree_util.py:docstring
#: of pybamm.expression_tree.tree_util.replace:12
msgid "Memo shared between calls made with the same ``mapping``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pybamm/expression_tree/tree_util.py:docstring
#: of pybamm.expression_tree.tree_util.replace:14
msgid ""
"Whether rebuilt operators apply their usual simplifications (default True)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/api/expression_tree/tree_util.rst:31
msgid "Migrating in-place updates"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/api/expression_tree/tree_util.rst:33
msgid ""
"Public symbol setters remain available but emit "
"``SymbolMutationDeprecationWarning``. ``children``, ``domain`` and "
"``input_names`` return immutable tuples that compare equal to lists, and "
"``domains`` returns a read-only copy: editing them raises ``TypeError``, and "
"not even ``list`` or ``dict`` methods can change the symbol through them. "
"Prefer constructing replacements::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/api/expression_tree/tree_util.rst:40
msgid ""
"updated = variable.create_copy(scale=2, reference=0, bounds=(0, 1))\n"
"expression = pybamm.replace(expression, {variable: updated})\n"
"symbol = symbol.with_domains({\"primary\": [\"negative electrode\"]})\n"
"symbol = symbol.without_domains()\n"
"symbol = symbol.with_mesh(mesh)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/api/expression_tree/tree_util.rst:46
msgid ""
"For names, scalar values and function inputs, construct a new symbol of the "
"appropriate class. IDs update automatically; callers need not call "
"``set_id``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/api/expression_tree/tree_util.rst:49
msgid ""
"Deprecated updates invalidate cached IDs and derived values across live "
"symbols. This deliberately slow compatibility path adds no per-symbol "
"tracking to normal replacement. Mutating symbols already used as dictionary "
"keys cannot repair those dictionaries: use a fresh replacement memo and "
"rebuild any parameter-processed or discretised model after legacy edits. "
"Changes to a child's domains do not propagate into constructor-derived "
"parent domains; reconstruct those expressions as well. Legacy mutation is "
"rejected while ``gc.freeze()`` is active because frozen ancestors cannot be "
"discovered for cache invalidation; use out-of-place replacement or unfreeze "
"the collector first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/api/expression_tree/tree_util.rst:59
msgid ""
"The test suite forbids deprecated mutation even with warnings ignored. Only "
"isolated compatibility subprocesses exercise the legacy path; notebook "
"kernels inherit the same guard as other tests. The guard "
"(``PYBAMM_TEST_FORBID_SYMBOL_MUTATION=1``) makes every deprecated public "
"update raise. A symbol's private slots, such as ``symbol._name``, are not "
"part of the API and writing them is unsupported: rather than intercept every "
"attribute write at runtime, the test suite checks PyBaMM's own code, tests, "
"examples and documentation for such writes statically."
msgstr ""
